From: ub82af643aafe86d2 at groups.google.com (Bill Harris)
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2014 18:41:33 +0000
Subject: Translate SQL involving two tables into plyr (or ddply)
Message-ID: <gviW8lwCCzI.WYCa35UputgJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/gviW8lwCCzI/m/WYCa35UputgJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I've got a problem I can express in SQL but haven't figured out how to express in dplyr.

## The Setup:
library(plyr)
library(sqldf)
library(lubridate)
df1 <- data.frame(
    entity = rep(c("A","B","C"),each = 3),
    date1 = c(
        ymd("2014-01-02"),  # A
        ymd("2014-01-07"),
        ymd("2014-01-15"),
        ymd("2014-01-04"),  # B
        ymd("2014-01-09"),
        ymd("2014-01-13"),
        ymd("2014-01-03"),  # C
        ymd("2014-01-08"),
        ymd("2014-01-14")),
    date2 = c(
        ymd("2014-01-06"),  # A
        ymd("2014-01-14"),
        ymd("2014-01-20"),
        ymd("2014-01-08"),  # B
        ymd("2014-01-12"),
        ymd("2014-01-19"),
        ymd("2014-01-07"),  # C
        ymd("2014-01-13"),
        ymd("2014-01-21")))
df1 <- mutate(df1, date1=round_date(date1,'day'),date2=round_date(date2,'day'))
df2 <- data.frame(
    datestamp = ymd("2014-01-01")+days(0:22),
    data = 1:23)
df1 <- mutate(df1, date1adj = round_date(date1 - days(1), 'day'),
              date2adj = round_date(date2 - days(1), 'day'))

## The Query:
q3b <- sqldf("select df1.entity, df1.date1, df1.date2,
              (select sum(data) from df2 where datestamp between df1.date1adj and df1.date2)
              as periodsums from df1")

Is there a reasonable way to express that in dplyr (or even plyr)?  Is it likely to be faster?  My real df1 has over 100,000 rows.

Thanks,

Bill

